We are probably the black sheep of eight thirty to nine thirty on network TV because what the fuck were we doing with this guy making it rain?
我们可能是网络电视上八点三十分到九点三十分的害群之马，因为我们他妈的和这个下雨的家伙做了什么？

00:38:57.900 --> 00:38:59.980
Hey, Howie Mandel was making it rain.
嘿，豪伊曼德尔正在下雨。

00:39:02.619 --> 00:39:05.627
Every night he was making it rain.
每天晚上他都会下雨。

00:39:05.627 --> 00:39:06.778
So much rain.
这么大的雨。

00:39:06.778 --> 00:39:10.139
The best kind of rain is a green kind.
最好的雨是绿色的雨。

00:39:10.139 --> 00:39:23.849
If we've gotten canceled after season one, I think we would have been, you know, it would have been another Jason Segal classic that got canceled after one season.
如果我们在第一季后被取消，我想我们会是，你知道，这将是杰森·西格尔的另一部经典作品，在一季后被取消。

00:39:23.849 --> 00:39:27.690
You know, like it would have been, I think a kind of freaks and geeks.
你知道，就像它本来应该的那样，我认为是一种怪胎和极客。

00:39:27.690 --> 00:39:31.130
A noble, a failover where the network gets kicked.
一个贵族，一个网络被踢的故障转移。

00:39:31.130 --> 00:39:46.949
But for some weird cosmic reason, it feels like because we, through some sort of, I don't know what kept us on the air, but there was something I think we were more on the bubble than we thought we were.
但出于某种奇怪的宇宙原因，感觉就像是因为我们通过某种方式，我不知道是什么让我们保持在空中，但我认为我们比我们想象的更处于泡沫之中。

00:39:46.949 --> 00:39:47.949
We were on the bubble.
我们正处于泡沫之中。

00:39:47.949 --> 00:39:49.849
We were definitely on the bubble.
我们确实处于泡沫之中。

00:39:49.849 --> 00:39:50.849
Here's the end of that story.
故事到这里就结束了。

00:39:50.849 --> 00:39:54.690
We're in this big conference room with this huge table full of people.
我们在一个大会议室里，桌子上坐满了人。

00:39:54.690 --> 00:39:57.690
It was the heads of the studio, the heads of the network.
这是工作室的负责人，网络的负责人。

00:39:57.690 --> 00:40:07.769
And we are to remind me of that scene where Joe Pashi and Goodfellas, he thinks he's walking in to become a made man and have this great positive meeting and then instead he's assassinated.
我们要提醒我那个场景，乔·帕希和古德费拉斯，他认为他走进来成为一个成功的人，并进行了一次伟大的积极的会面，然后他却被暗杀了。

00:40:07.769 --> 00:40:14.289
That was how the meeting felt a little bit, or Carter and I were a little bit like, oh, this is not the meeting we thought.
这就是会议的感觉，或者卡特和我有点像，哦，这不是我们想象的会议。

00:40:14.289 --> 00:40:21.610
And we were just told like be less serialized, be less emo, more standalone episodes, come on and you have a great cast, don't throw this thing away.
我们只是被告知要少一些连续剧，少一些情绪化，多一些独立剧集，来吧，你有一个很棒的演员阵容，不要扔掉这个东西。

00:40:21.610 --> 00:40:27.610
Don't throw this thing away by being so heady and emotional and intricately serialized, all that kind of stuff.
不要因为如此令人陶醉、情绪化、错综复杂的连载之类的东西而把它扔掉。

00:40:27.610 --> 00:40:33.989
Flash forward to season two, we didn't stop doing any of that stuff if anything we did it more.
快进到第二季，我们并没有停止做任何这些事情，如果我们做得更多的话。

00:40:33.989 --> 00:40:38.989
So the point of my story is stick to your guns.
所以我的故事的重点是坚持你的立场。

00:40:40.070 --> 00:40:55.090
The point of the story is we believed that the audience was there for this type of show with this tone, maybe our ratings had dipped a little, maybe we were gonna be a slow burn, maybe we were gonna have people find us and we just had to hang out till that happened.
这个故事的重点是，我们相信观众会以这种基调观看这种类型的节目，也许我们的收视率下降了一点，也许我们会慢慢燃烧，也许我们会让人找到我们，而我们只能坚持到那件事发生。

00:40:55.090 --> 00:40:58.710
It started to happen more in season two, it started to happen more in season three.
它在第二季开始发生更多，在第三季开始发生更多。

00:40:58.710 --> 00:41:01.789
The show got on Netflix, that really made it start to happen.
该剧在 Netflix 上播出，这才真正开始发生。

00:41:01.789 --> 00:41:14.269
And all of a sudden everyone was consuming television in the way that rewarded serialized storytelling, emotional storytelling, intricate, playful, curious, weird, abstract, creative storytelling.
突然间，每个人都以奖励连载故事、情感故事、复杂、有趣、好奇、怪异、抽象、创造性的故事的方式消费电视。

00:41:14.269 --> 00:41:16.510
And we just were able to weather that storm.
我们刚刚度过了这场风暴。

00:41:16.510 --> 00:41:23.309
And again, by that point, all those same people who had expressed that concern at the end of season one kind of went, we get it.
到那时，所有那些在赛季结束时表达过这种担忧的人都走了，我们明白了。

00:41:23.309 --> 00:41:25.909
We see what you're doing and it's working.
我们看到您在做什么并且它正在发挥作用。

00:41:25.909 --> 00:41:27.670
And they did stick by us.
他们确实支持我们。

00:41:27.670 --> 00:41:29.349
Carter and I thought we were gonna get fired.
卡特和我以为我们会被解雇。

00:41:29.349 --> 00:41:35.550
We didn't even necessarily think the show was gonna get canceled, but we're like, are we gonna get fired off our own show, which has happened?
我们甚至不一定认为这个节目会被取消，但我们想，我们自己的节目会被解雇吗，这已经发生了？

00:41:35.550 --> 00:41:41.150
Because it's like, the feeling was you're squandering this opportunity because you're telling stories in this crazy way.
因为感觉就像你在浪费这个机会，因为你用这种疯狂的方式讲故事。

00:41:41.150 --> 00:41:47.190
And we disagreed, a pan-fryment disagreed, you guys, the cast disagreed, you all had faith in us.
我们不同意，煎锅不同意，你们，演员们不同意，你们都对我们有信心。

00:41:47.190 --> 00:41:49.389
And we basically just doubled down and kept doing it.
我们基本上只是加倍努力并继续这样做。

00:41:49.389 --> 00:41:51.309
We didn't change much of anything in season two.
我们在第二季中没有做太多改变。

00:41:51.309 --> 00:41:53.670
If anything, we just did it more.
如果说有什么不同的话，那就是我们做得更多了。

00:41:53.670 --> 00:41:59.210
So I'm very proud that we stuck with what the vision was, and I'm so happy it worked out in the end.
因此，我非常自豪我们坚持了最初的愿景，而且我很高兴最终实现了这一目标。

00:41:59.210 --> 00:42:03.969
Well, it's almost like TV shows are not unlike romance, right?
好吧，这就像电视节目和浪漫故事没什么不同，对吧？

00:42:03.969 --> 00:42:10.530
Where things can line up, they can be the right people wrong time, right?
只要事情能够协调一致，他们就可以在错误的时间成为正确的人，对吗？

00:42:10.530 --> 00:42:18.849
And so much had to break our way, like truly, like I remember when we went on Netflix.
确实有太多事情需要打破我们的道路，就像我记得我们看 Netflix 时那样。

00:42:18.849 --> 00:42:27.369
And it was, I remember breaking bad was kind of a quiet, critically beloved, but kind of quiet show.
我记得《绝命毒师》是一部安静的、受到批判性喜爱的、但又安静的节目。

00:42:27.369 --> 00:42:30.489
And then it went on Netflix and it just became a phenomenon.
然后它在 Netflix 上播出并成为一种现象。

00:42:30.489 --> 00:42:33.170
And a similar thing happened to us.
类似的事情也发生在我们身上。

00:42:33.170 --> 00:42:37.530
I do remember very strongly, I think it was fourth season.
我记得很清楚，我想那是第四季。

00:42:37.530 --> 00:42:43.130
We were sitting around on a Tuesday waiting to start or maybe we were waiting for the execs to come.
我们在周二坐在那里等待开始，或者也许我们在等待高管来。

00:42:43.130 --> 00:42:43.969
I think it was that.
我想就是这样。

00:42:43.969 --> 00:42:48.690
We were waiting for everyone to come down for a tablery, I mean for the run through.
我们正在等待每个人下来吃桌子，我的意思是为了进行跑步。

00:42:48.690 --> 00:42:53.710
And I remember Jason said to us, are things getting weird for you guys out here?
我记得杰森对我们说，你们这里的事情变得奇怪了吗？

00:42:53.710 --> 00:42:54.550
Anyone else?
还有其他人吗？

00:42:54.550 --> 00:43:22.210
like meaning he was getting recognized for the show more than ever and before we always said we were like this sleepy little sleeper we were we were beloved by the people that were watching but otherwise we were whatever but when it went on Netflix people just caught it it started spreading around we all started to feel like we were more on a hit television show than we had ever felt we hadn't felt that the first three seasons and so much had to go right it was like we had all the the right elements.
就像这意味着他比以往任何时候都更能获得这部剧的认可，之前我们总是说我们就像这个昏昏欲睡的小睡者，我们受到观众的喜爱，但除此之外我们什么都不是，但当它在Netflix上播出时，人们刚刚发现它开始传播开来，我们都开始觉得我们比以往任何时候都更像是一部热门电视节目，我们不觉得前三季和那么多事情都必须顺利进行，就好像我们拥有所有正确的元素一样。

00:43:22.210 --> 00:43:26.756
I think what the executives were saying was we know we have something special here.
我认为高管们所说的是我们知道我们这里有一些特别的东西。

00:43:26.756 --> 00:43:32.453
They were just trying to figure out how to keep it, you know, to make it blaze a little brighter, right?
他们只是想弄清楚如何保持它，你知道，让它变得更亮一点，对吗？

00:43:32.453 --> 00:43:33.822
I genuinely believe that.
我真心相信这一点。

00:43:33.822 --> 00:43:35.575
I really do think they loved it.
我真的认为他们喜欢它。

00:43:35.575 --> 00:43:38.478
They were good people and they did stick by the show.
他们都是好人，而且确实坚持演出。

00:43:38.478 --> 00:43:46.803
They were concerned at that one moment and the ending is happy because these were executives that did stick with believing in us, believing in the show.
他们在那一刻很担心，但结局是幸福的，因为这些高管确实坚持相信我们，相信这个节目。

00:43:46.803 --> 00:43:49.213
I feel like the show was doing a rain dance.
我感觉这个节目在跳雨舞。

00:43:49.213 --> 00:43:57.429
The show itself was doing Ted's rain dance on the roof saying, And please come on, come on, come on, and the universe, it delivered for us in the end.
节目本身就是特德在屋顶上跳雨舞，说道：“来吧，来吧，来吧，宇宙最终为我们带来了。”

00:43:57.429 --> 00:43:58.429
And thank you.
谢谢你。

00:43:58.429 --> 00:43:59.429
And thank you.
谢谢你。

00:43:59.429 --> 00:44:00.429
Honestly, thank you to the fans.
说实话，谢谢粉丝们。

00:44:00.429 --> 00:44:01.429
Yeah.
是的。

00:44:01.429 --> 00:44:08.389
Well, why don't we, let's go through, like, these were kind of my notes that I really liked.
好吧，我们为什么不，让我们看一下，这些是我真正喜欢的笔记。

