01:16:56.979 --> 01:16:58.939
Thanks, Cassandra, that's so lovely.
谢谢，卡桑德拉，太可爱了。

01:16:58.939 --> 01:17:00.739
That's meant to have been Kira Johnson's thing about it.
这本来就是基拉·约翰逊的事。

01:17:00.739 --> 01:17:01.819
I don't care, right?
我不在乎，对吧？

01:17:01.819 --> 01:17:08.020
Sorry, Kira, Kira, you can follow up, but we don't know, you got to, you left us hanging, here we go.
抱歉，基拉，基拉，你可以跟进，但我们不知道，你必须这样做，你让我们悬而未决，我们开始吧。

01:17:08.020 --> 01:17:12.659
We're going to open season two with a further explanation from Kira.
我们将在基拉的进一步解释下开始第二季。

01:17:12.659 --> 01:17:15.260
The reveal, once the missing sentence there.
揭晓，曾经缺失的那句话。

01:17:15.260 --> 01:17:23.275
David Anthony writes, I think it is also so loved because they captured a moment before two major changes, major changes, major changes.
大卫·安东尼写道，我认为它也如此受欢迎，因为他们捕捉到了两个重大变化之前的一个时刻，重大变化，重大变化。

01:17:23.275 --> 01:17:33.470
One is the sort of preceding the death of cable TV and sitcoms about young 20 something's figuring it out as things transition to streaming and overly dramatic bingeable TV.
一种是有线电视消亡之前的类型，以及关于 20 岁左右的年轻人在事情转向流媒体和过于戏剧性的狂欢电视时解决问题的情景喜剧。

01:17:33.470 --> 01:17:37.595
The second is that it captures life in the sweet spot of the internet.
第二是它抓住了互联网的最佳状态。

01:17:37.595 --> 01:17:40.778
It was there and used, but it was not our entire life.
它在那里并被使用，但这并不是我们生活的全部。

01:17:40.778 --> 01:17:42.899
We go on it and and then got off it.
我们继续前进，然后又下车。

01:17:42.899 --> 01:17:46.140
And we still interacted with each other in real life and made plans.
而我们在现实生活中仍然互动并制定计划。

01:17:46.140 --> 01:17:53.100
So it's not just the romance of the show, but the romance of a time before these inventions changed who we are and how we live.
所以这不仅仅是剧中的浪漫，而是这些发明改变我们是谁和我们生活方式之前的浪漫。

01:17:53.100 --> 01:17:54.899
I think that is brilliant.
我认为这太棒了。

01:17:54.899 --> 01:17:58.659
I haven't really thought about that, but that is such a great insight.
我还没有真正考虑过这一点，但这真是一个伟大的见解。

01:17:58.659 --> 01:18:00.500
Thank you for that, David.
谢谢你，大卫。

01:18:00.500 --> 01:18:02.899
Yeah, it's there, but it's not everything.
是的，它就在那里，但它并不是一切。

01:18:02.899 --> 01:18:03.739
I love that.
我喜欢那个。

01:18:03.739 --> 01:18:04.819
Thank you, David, brilliant.
谢谢你，大卫，太棒了。

01:18:06.220 --> 01:18:15.020
Sanjay says, like Marshall talks to Stella about Ted's relationship with Star Wars, and how he watches the movies when he's happy, sick, et cetera.
桑杰说，就像马歇尔与斯特拉谈论泰德与星球大战的关系，以及他在快乐、生病等时如何看电影一样。

01:18:15.020 --> 01:18:17.739
The same is for me with how I met your mother.
我和你母亲的认识也是如此。

01:18:17.739 --> 01:18:21.460
I lost count of how many times I watched the series from beginning to end.
我已经记不清这部剧从头到尾看了多少遍了。

01:18:21.460 --> 01:18:25.100
There are days that I'm in a special mood and I watch a very specific episode.
有时候我心情特别好，会观看非常具体的一集。

01:18:25.100 --> 01:18:37.189
This show helped me in my worst times, kept me company during my sleepless nights, made me laugh and cry uncontrollably many, many times since I bumped into it by accident on TV back in 2008.
自从2008年我在电视上偶然看到这个节目以来，这个节目在我最糟糕的时候帮助了我，在我不眠之夜陪伴了我，让我无法控制地笑和哭了很多很多次。

01:18:37.189 --> 01:18:40.069
And the final letter from Hello Leesh.
还有你好利什的最后一封信。

01:18:40.069 --> 01:18:46.909
I so appreciate when you guys recognize that this show belongs to the fans, perhaps more than it belongs to those who created it.
当你们认识到这个节目属于粉丝，也许比它属于创作者的时候，我非常感激。

01:18:46.909 --> 01:18:49.590
It took me a while to recognize that this is the case.
我花了一段时间才意识到情况确实如此。

01:18:49.590 --> 01:19:02.510
In all honesty, I've been frustrated when an actor doesn't remember one of their iconic lines when asked in an interview, or when one of the show's writers gives an opinion about one of the characters that defies all the analysis I've done of that character for decades.
老实说，当一位演员在采访中被问到时不记得他们的标志性台词之一，或者当该剧的一位编剧对其中一个角色给出的看法违背了我几十年来对该角色所做的所有分析时，我感到很沮丧。

01:19:02.510 --> 01:19:05.449
And then I realize this belongs to the fans.
然后我意识到这属于粉丝。

01:19:05.449 --> 01:19:08.710
No one has watched and analyzed these stories as much as the fans have.
没有人像粉丝一样关注和分析这些故事。

01:19:08.710 --> 01:19:12.510
It's the fans that are the keepers of these stories, these characters and their souls.
粉丝是这些故事、这些角色及其灵魂的守护者。

01:19:12.510 --> 01:19:18.069
The soul of the show itself continues to live in the hearts and minds and lives of the people who love it dearly.
该节目本身的灵魂继续活在深爱它的人们的心中、思想和生活中。

01:19:18.069 --> 01:19:32.550
And just like an artist can put her love and care and spirit into creating a painting, if that painting is passed on to a new owner, it's quite likely the owner will come to love and know that painting, particularly from studying and appreciating it daily, more than the creator of said art.
就像艺术家可以将自己的爱、关怀和精神投入到创作一幅画中一样，如果这幅画被传给了新的主人，那么主人很可能会比该艺术的创作者更喜欢和了解这幅画，特别是通过每天的学习和欣赏。

01:19:32.550 --> 01:19:39.331
The spirit that went into that thing is amplified or diminished depending on how much the keeper loves appreciates it.
进入那个东西的精神会被放大或减弱，这取决于守护者对它的喜爱程度和欣赏程度。

01:19:39.331 --> 01:19:46.860
And the reason this show is so magical is because there is a band of keepers that continue to nourish the soul of this work of art.
而这场展览之所以如此神奇，是因为有一群守护者在不断滋养着这件艺术作品的灵魂。

01:19:46.860 --> 01:19:50.654
Thank you for not only creating it, but for passing it down to us.
感谢您不仅创造了它，而且感谢您将它传递给我们。

01:19:50.654 --> 01:19:54.390
You may never know how much this means to so many people's lives.
您可能永远不知道这对这么多人的生活意味着什么。

01:19:55.689 --> 01:19:59.718
Well, we are getting to know it from letters like that.
嗯，我们是从这样的信件中了解到这一点的。

01:19:59.718 --> 01:20:10.850
And I'm just humbled, Craig, to have to have been a part of something that means this much to people, and also to create it with someone I like so much.
克雷格，我很荣幸能够成为对人们意义重大的事物的一部分，并且与我非常喜欢的人一起创造它。

01:20:10.850 --> 01:20:13.250
I just love you, my friend.
我只是爱你，我的朋友。

01:20:13.250 --> 01:20:24.250
And when I thought about who I wanna walk down memory lane with, you were the person that I wanted to do it with, you and I have always had a sweet and special connection.
当我想到我想和谁一起走在记忆的路上时，你就是我想和他一起走的人，你和我一直有着甜蜜而特殊的联系。

01:20:24.250 --> 01:20:38.890
I know that Ted was based on Carter, and I think it's funny that the guy who was playing the Carter felt this ease of friendship with you, who was the Marshall, because Ted and Marshall love each other, you know, and I love you always.
我知道泰德是以卡特为原型的，我觉得很有趣的是，扮演卡特的那个人与你（马歇尔）感受到了这种轻松的友谊，因为泰德和马歇尔彼此相爱，你知道，我永远爱你。

01:20:38.890 --> 01:20:46.569
And I'm grateful that we are getting to have this second life professionally together by revisiting this thing we made.
我很感激我们能够通过重新审视我们所做的事情来共同获得职业上的第二次生命。

01:20:46.569 --> 01:20:54.529
And I just think you're the sweetest, specialist, funniest, kindest dude, and I'm just so grateful you're in my life.
我只是认为你是最可爱、最专业、最有趣、最善良的家伙，我非常感激你出现在我的生命中。

01:20:54.529 --> 01:20:56.050
Oh man, thanks Josh.
噢，伙计，谢谢乔希。

01:20:56.050 --> 01:20:58.609
I'm very moved by that, thanks buddy.
我很感动，谢谢朋友。

01:20:58.609 --> 01:21:00.250
I filled the exact same way about you.
我对你也用同样的方式填写。

01:21:00.250 --> 01:21:11.050
how lucky that you walked into Carter in my office in 2005 and were Ted Mosby and you were the guy and you became our dear, dear friend.
多么幸运，2005 年你在我的办公室遇到了卡特，你就是特德·莫斯比，你就是那个人，你成为了我们亲爱的、亲爱的朋友。

01:21:11.050 --> 01:21:12.289
We loved you then.
那时我们爱你。

01:21:12.289 --> 01:21:13.970
We love you now.
我们现在爱你。

01:21:13.970 --> 01:21:24.130
There's no show without you and getting to go back on this journey with you and celebrate our friendship and all the friendship we shared with everybody that created the show.
没有你们就没有演出，我们可以和你们一起回到这段旅程，庆祝我们的友谊，以及我们与创作该节目的每个人分享的所有友谊。

01:21:24.130 --> 01:21:26.890
It's really special and I really need it right now.
它真的很特别，我现在真的需要它。

01:21:26.890 --> 01:21:35.609
I think I keep hearing from fans that say, I like this right now, I need this moment, I need this time travel, I need this little break from what the world feels like.
我想我不断听到粉丝们说，我喜欢现在，我需要这一刻，我需要这次时间旅行，我需要暂时脱离现实世界。

01:21:35.609 --> 01:21:39.729
And it's really a gift to get that with you, Josh.
乔什，能把它带在身边真是一份礼物。

01:21:39.729 --> 01:21:41.609
So thank you for inviting me on that journey.
所以谢谢你邀请我踏上这段旅程。

01:21:41.609 --> 01:21:49.010
And thanks to Gerdana too, because I really think it sparked from her in a lot of ways and sparked from your marriage and it sparked from where you are in your life right now.
还要感谢格尔达娜，因为我真的认为这在很多方面都源于她，源于你的婚姻，源于你现在的生活。

01:21:49.010 --> 01:21:52.649
So thank you for letting me continue to be a part of your life, my friend.
所以，谢谢你让我继续成为你生活的一部分，我的朋友。

01:21:52.649 --> 01:21:53.489
I love you.
我爱你。

01:21:53.489 --> 01:21:54.409
Love you too, brother.
也爱你，兄弟。

01:21:54.409 --> 01:21:56.529
Hey, Alec, we love you too, my friend.
嘿，亚历克，我们也爱你，我的朋友。

01:21:56.529 --> 01:21:57.569
And I love you guys.
我爱你们。

01:21:57.569 --> 01:22:01.362
Thank you so much for- you don't look anything like I was picturing.
非常感谢你——你看起来一点也不像我想象的那样。

01:22:01.362 --> 01:22:03.370
We'll see you next season, everyone.
大家，我们下赛季再见。

01:22:03.370 --> 01:22:06.103
Thanks so much for going on this journey with us.
非常感谢您与我们一起踏上这段旅程。

01:22:06.103 --> 01:22:06.603
Thanks.
谢谢。

01:22:06.603 --> 01:22:07.719
See you next season.
下赛季见。

